    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d887">

                <pb facs="1101" n="1091" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg1091"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/3–1747</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Director of the Office of Far Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Vincent</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Under Secretary of State for Economic Affairs</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Clayton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1947-03-17">March 17, 1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I am attaching a copy of a memorandum<anchor n="10" xml:id="d887-f1"/> which I
                    sent to General Marshall last Friday together with a copy of his
                        instruction<anchor n="11" xml:id="d887-f2"/> which caused me to take the
                    action reported in my memorandum.</p>
                <p>The prospects of favorable action are clearly not encouraging, but knowing how
                    earnestly the Secretary desires that something be done I think that we ought to
                    leave no stone unturned here in trying to do something. Incidentally, he spent
                    an hour with me the day before his departure talking over this matter.</p>
                <p>I am also attaching a copy of my earlier memorandum<anchor n="12"
                        xml:id="d887-f3"/> and Bennett’s memorandum<anchor n="13" xml:id="d887-f4"/>
                    to which the General refers in his instruction to me. These memoranda grew out
                    of an earlier conversation I had with him.</p>
                <p>I should like to talk to you about this as soon as you can conveniently arrange
                    the time. You will note that I have sent copies of my memorandum to the
                    Secretary to Mr. Thorp<anchor n="14" xml:id="d887-f5"/> and Mr. Ness.<anchor
                        n="15" xml:id="d887-f6"/> It will be helpful if they could be present at our
                    meeting.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ohn</hi>] C[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >arter</hi>] V[<hi rendition="#small-caps">incent</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
